From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rve build fix <noreply@example.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] libc: guard adjtimex against missing __NR_adjtimex

On riscv32, Linux never defined __NR_adjtimex because RISC-V uses
64-bit time_t from the start (y2038-safe ABI). __ARCH_WANT_TIME32_SYSCALLS
is not set for RISC-V, so the asm-generic header omits __NR_adjtimex.

Guard the _syscall1 expansion with #ifdef __NR_adjtimex and fall back
to ENOSYS so the build succeeds on riscv32 with 6.x kernel headers.
---
 libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c | 8 +++++++-
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c b/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c
+++ b/libc/sysdeps/linux/common/adjtimex.c
@@ -11,3 +11,9 @@


-_syscall1(int, adjtimex, struct timex *, buf)
+#ifdef __NR_adjtimex
+_syscall1(int, adjtimex, struct timex *, buf)
+#else
+#include <errno.h>
+int adjtimex(struct timex *buf) { errno = ENOSYS; return -1; }
+#endif
 libc_hidden_def(adjtimex)
--
